<p id="S2.Thmthm1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.Thmthm1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> represents the fundamental class.</p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1. </span>Compact type and rational tails</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A stable curve is of compact type if its dual graph has no cycles.
We say it is a curve with rational tails if it has one irreducible component of full genus, because then all other components are chains (tails) of rational curves.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We consider Deligne’s pushforward weight spectral sequence in the cases
<math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{\mathrm{ct}}_{g,n}\subset\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>ct</mi></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{\mathrm{ct}}_{g,n}\subset\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math>
and
<math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{\mathrm{rt}}_{g,n}\subset\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>rt</mi></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{\mathrm{rt}}_{g,n}\subset\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The first page of the spectral sequence is similar to the one for
<math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{g,n}\subset\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{g,n}\subset\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The difference is that in the case of curves of compact type we sum over stable graphs without bridges and
in the case of curves with rational tails we sum over stable graphs without any rational tails.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3. </span>Deligne’s pullback weight spectral sequence</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When doing concrete computations, it is helpful to use both Deligne’s pushforward weight spectral sequence and its Poincaré dual version, which has an <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-page of the form,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{E}_{1}^{p,q}=\bigoplus_{|E_{\Gamma}|=p}\bigl(H^{q}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{\Gamma})\otimes\mathrm{det}(E_{\Gamma})\bigr)^{\mathrm{Aut}(\Gamma)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⨁</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>det</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>Aut</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{E}_{1}^{p,q}=\bigoplus_{|E_{\Gamma}|=p}\bigl(H^{q}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{\Gamma})\otimes\mathrm{det}(E_{\Gamma})\bigr)^{\mathrm{Aut}(\Gamma)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, Example 3.5]</cite>. This spectral sequence also degenerates at the second page and abuts to the weight <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> graded piece,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{E}_{2}^{p,q}=\mathrm{gr}_{q}H_{c}^{p+q}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>gr</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{E}_{2}^{p,q}=\mathrm{gr}_{q}H_{c}^{p+q}(\mathcal{M}_{g,n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Fixing <math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, the complex <math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{E}_{1}^{p,q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{E}_{1}^{p,q}</annotation></semantics></math> can also be identified with the Getzler-Kapranov complex <math id="S3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{GK}^{q}_{g,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>GK</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{GK}^{q}_{g,n}</annotation></semantics></math>. For more details see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, Section 2.3]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>.
Similarly to Section <a href="#S2" title="2. Deligne’s pushforward weight spectral sequence ‣ Deligne’s weight spectral sequence and tautological cohomology of the moduli space of curves" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the differential</p>
<table id="S3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{1}:\tilde{E}_{1}^{p,q}\rightarrow\tilde{E}_{1}^{p+1,q}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{1}:\tilde{E}_{1}^{p,q}\rightarrow\tilde{E}_{1}^{p+1,q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">restricted to a graph <math id="S3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mapsto\sum_{v\in V_{\Gamma}}\sum_{\hat{\Gamma}}\frac{1}{|\mathrm{Aut}(\hat{\Gamma}^{\prime})|}\sum_{\psi\in\mathrm{Aut}(\hat{\Gamma}^{\prime})}\textrm{sgn}(\sigma_{\hat{\Gamma},\psi})\cdot(\psi\circ\phi\circ\xi_{\hat{\Gamma},\Gamma})^{*}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Aut</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Aut</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mtext>sgn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mapsto\sum_{v\in V_{\Gamma}}\sum_{\hat{\Gamma}}\frac{1}{|\mathrm{Aut}(\hat{\Gamma}^{\prime})|}\sum_{\psi\in\mathrm{Aut}(\hat{\Gamma}^{\prime})}\textrm{sgn}(\sigma_{\hat{\Gamma},\psi})\cdot(\psi\circ\phi\circ\xi_{\hat{\Gamma},\Gamma})^{*}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Here the second sum is over all stable graphs <math id="S3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> obtained by either splitting the vertex <math id="S3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> or adding a loop to the vertex <math id="S3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and lowering its genus by one.
This operation is dual to contracting an edge in the sense that by contracting this new edge of <math id="S3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain <math id="S3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> again.
From the ordering of <math id="S3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> we inherit the ordering <math id="S3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\hat{\Gamma}}:E_{\hat{\Gamma}}\rightarrow\{1,\ldots,|E_{\Gamma}|+1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\hat{\Gamma}}:E_{\hat{\Gamma}}\rightarrow\{1,\ldots,|E_{\Gamma}|+1\}</annotation></semantics></math> obtained by sending the new edge to <math id="S3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|E_{\Gamma}|+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|E_{\Gamma}|+1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Gamma}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Gamma}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be the chosen representative of the isomorphism class of <math id="S3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> and fix an isomorphism <math id="S3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\hat{\Gamma}\rightarrow\hat{\Gamma}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\hat{\Gamma}\rightarrow\hat{\Gamma}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Now <math id="S3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\hat{\Gamma},\psi}:=\alpha_{\hat{\Gamma}^{\prime}}\circ\psi_{E}\circ\phi_{E}\circ\gamma^{-1}_{\hat{\Gamma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\hat{\Gamma},\psi}:=\alpha_{\hat{\Gamma}^{\prime}}\circ\psi_{E}\circ\phi_{E}\circ\gamma^{-1}_{\hat{\Gamma}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma=\hbox to51.9pt{\vbox to11.71pt{\pgfpicture\makeatletter\hbox{\hskip 25.94899pt\lower-4.60942pt\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin} \lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill} \lxSVG@setlinewidth{\the\pgflinewidth}\lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke-width} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\nullfont\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin} {{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}}
